<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tegucigalpa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tegucigalpa is the capital and largest city of Honduras, in a highland valley of the south-centre. It grew from a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>-mining settlement founded in 1578, and after independence it rivalled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comayagua">Comayagua</a> as the seat of government until it became the permanent capital in 1880. Together with neighbouring Comayagüela it forms the Central District.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tegucigalpa.jpg" alt="Tegucigalpa" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Inforgetmenots · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tegucigalpa_downtown_panoramic_2026.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
